== Shareholders ==
Deutsche Bank is one of the leading listed companies in German post-war history. Its shares are traded on the [[Frankfurt Stock Exchange]] and, since 2001, also on the [[New York Stock Exchange]] and are included in various indices, including the [[DAX]] and the [[Euro Stoxx 50]]. As the share had lost value since mid-2015 and market capitalization had shrunk to around €18&nbsp;billion, it temporarily withdrew from the Euro Stoxx 50 on 8 August 2016.<ref>{{cite news |date=2 August 2016 |title=Ehemaliges Top-Geldhaus fliegt aus Stoxx 50: Fast Exit für die Deutsche Bank |url=http://www.manager-magazin.de/unternehmen/banken/deutsche-bank-fliegt-aus-stoxx-europe-50-a-1105736.html |work=[[manager magazin]] |access-date=25 May 2026 |language=de}}</ref> With a 0.73% stake, it is currently the company with the lowest index weighting.<ref>{{cite web |title=EURO STOXX 50® INDEX |url=https://www.stoxx.com/document/Indices/Factsheets_Components/2018/July/SX5E.pdf |publisher=[[STOXX]] |format=PDF |access-date=25 May 2026}}</ref> In 2001, Deutsche Bank merged its mortgage banking business with that of [[Dresdner Bank]] and [[Commerzbank]] to form [[Eurohypo|Eurohypo AG]]. In 2005, Deutsche Bank sold its stake in the joint company to Commerzbank.<ref>{{cite web |date=26 March 2007 |title=Related Party Transactions |url=https://annualreport.deutsche-bank.com/2006/ar/supplementaryinformation/corporategovernancereport/reportingandtransparency/relatedpartytransactions/print.html |website=annualreport.deutsche-bank.com |publisher=Deutsche Bank |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190306044438/https://annualreport.deutsche-bank.com/2006/ar/supplementaryinformation/corporategovernancereport/reportingandtransparency/relatedpartytransactions/print.html |archive-date=6 March 2019 |access-date=25 May 2026 |language=en}}</ref>
